# British English Localisation

All text content in the Horsforth in Bloom website must use British English spelling and terminology.

## Common British English Spellings

### -ise vs -ize
- ✅ **Correct**: "organise", "realise", "recognise", "specialise"
- ❌ **Incorrect**: "organize", "realize", "recognize", "specialize"

### -our vs -or
- ✅ **Correct**: "colour", "favour", "honour", "behaviour", "neighbour"
- ❌ **Incorrect**: "color", "favor", "honor", "behavior", "neighbor"

### -re vs -er
- ✅ **Correct**: "centre", "theatre", "metre", "litre"
- ❌ **Incorrect**: "center", "theater", "meter", "liter"

### -ll vs -l
- ✅ **Correct**: "travelling", "modelling", "cancelled", "jewellery"
- ❌ **Incorrect**: "traveling", "modeling", "canceled", "jewelry"

### -ae/-oe vs -e
- ✅ **Correct**: "manoeuvre", "foetus", "paediatric"
- ❌ **Incorrect**: "maneuver", "fetus", "pediatric"

## British Terminology

### Time and Dates
- ✅ **Correct**: "autumn" (not "fall"), "fortnight", "bank holiday"
- ✅ **Correct**: "31st March" (not "March 31st")

### Measurements
- ✅ **Correct**: "metres", "kilometres", "centimetres"
- ✅ **Correct**: "tonnes" (not "tons")

### Common Words
- ✅ **Correct**: "car park" (not "parking lot")
- ✅ **Correct**: "pavement" (not "sidewalk")
- ✅ **Correct**: "lorry" (not "truck")
- ✅ **Correct**: "biscuit" (not "cookie")
- ✅ **Correct**: "crisps" (not "chips")

## Content Guidelines

### Community Context
- Use "community" rather than "neighborhood"
- Use "council" rather than "municipality"
- Use "volunteer" (consistent with American English)

### Gardening Terms
- Use "wildflower" (one word, consistent with American English)
- Use "planting" rather than "landscaping"
- Use "bed" for flower beds
- Use "roundabout" rather than "traffic circle"

## Implementation

When writing or editing content:
1. Always check spelling against British English standards
2. Use British terminology appropriate for UK context
3. Maintain consistency across all pages and components
4. Consider the local Horsforth/Leeds context when choosing terms

## Examples in Code

```tsx
// ✅ Correct British English
<p>We organise community planting events throughout the year.</p>
<p>The wildflower meadows provide beautiful colour in summer.</p>
<p>Our volunteers work in the town centre and surrounding areas.</p>

// ❌ Incorrect American English
<p>We organize community planting events throughout the year.</p>
<p>The wildflower meadows provide beautiful color in summer.</p>
<p>Our volunteers work in the town center and surrounding areas.</p>
```